  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R39 / cognitive C6 (block 330000): the COST & IMPACT of action -- the thermodynamics of agency. ac_work: a working agent with enough energy extracts from a Deposit (output=min(work_yield,stock), partial-take, no over-extraction) -> spends work_cost energy AND deposits output into the food Store. Work COSTS (energy down) and has IMPACT (store up); output CONSERVED from the deposit; empty deposit -> nothing; energy<work_cost -> can't work. ac_eat: a hungry agent with food consumes one unit (store.stock-1), reducing hunger + restoring energy -- recovering the drive COSTS a real resource that must exist (no free recovery, food conserved). ac_rest: restores energy (capped). ac_metabolize: per epoch energy drains + hunger rises (cost of living) -> forces the work->eat loop; idle agents run down. Nothing is free.",
